imapi2: add the disc master of a PC without an optical drive (Neutron#30)

Lightroom Classic crashed into Adobe's error report on Export To: CD/DVD. Its DiscBurning.dll creates
MsftDiscMaster2 and uses the object without checking the result; Wine had no imapi2.dll, so CoCreateInstance
returned REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG and Adobe read through a NULL pointer (access violation in DiscBurning.dll+0x2689,
RAX = 0x80040154). Windows always ships imapi2.dll.

New imapi2.dll with MsftDiscMaster2 (IDiscMaster2): a supported environment with no recorders, as Windows
reports on a PC without an optical drive. Recording itself (MsftDiscRecorder2, MsftDiscFormat2Data, ...) is not
implemented.

Tests: harness imapi2-master.c FAILS on 139 (class not registered) and PASSES with the DLL (supported, 0
recorders, empty enumeration). Lightroom Classic 15.6 (lab, 139 + this DLL): Export To: CD/DVD shows the CD/DVD
settings, and Export ends in Lightroom's own "Lightroom cannot burn data because it cannot locate a drive that
supports burning." — the Windows behavior without a burner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

